A||N||5||BruceV||Harness||||5||
Z||000000||BruceV||07-31-2001||09:15 PM||||Can any one tell me how to unplug the interior harness from the Eng. harness at the firewall??  Having trouble getting them unpluged.....||||reg||5
Z||000001||Jay||07-31-2001||09:19 PM||||They can be tough, especially if they haven't come off in a while.  Be careful but be firm.  There are tabs on the end of each connector, push them in and yank.  Try to pull on the plastic rather than on the wires themselves.  Hope this helps.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||07-31-2001||09:54 PM||||The engine harness connector is secured with a bolt.  Use a 1/4 inch socket and back out the bolt in the center of the plug.  The plug will begin to separate as the bolt is unscrewed.  The bolt is captive to the plug, so don't try to pull it all the way out.<BR>(I assume you're not talking about the "plug" where the wires go through the hole in the firewall.  It's not really a plug, it's a plastic grommet and is held in by a "C" shaped plastic clip on the interior side.)<BR>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Rodrv6 (edited 07-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||07-31-2001||11:28 PM||||Are you talking about the end inside the car or the one in the engine compartment?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tigger||07-31-2001||11:49 PM||||Where the harness passes through the firewall you have to remove a plastic clip that slides over that plastic thingy that the wires pass through.  You can get one clip off from inside, the other from the engine compartment.<P>You are not alone, I remember scratching my head for quite some trying to remove the harness at that plug and through the firewall.  uh, what fun.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 07-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||KRMFiero||08-01-2001||08:55 AM||||If it is the harness that i am thinking of, use a 7 mm socket and there will be a nut in the middle, undo that and then i think there are some tabs you have to flip also on each side||||reg||1
